# Files that must never enter the published archive.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# 0.7.3 shipped a 16,023,777-byte archive of which ~99.9% was a `build/`
# directory that had no business in a package. It held nine files, the largest a
# Flutter kernel cache (`build/test_cache/build/*.cache.dill.track.dill`,
# 49,014,912 bytes uncompressed) embedding 1,323 absolute paths from the
# publishing machine, plus 24 references to the temporary staging directory it
# was published from. Consumers who pulled 0.7.3 downloaded all of it.
#
# The cause was NOT a missing .gitignore rule. The repo-root .gitignore has
# ignored `**/build/` since 2026-03-04, and `pub publish` honours it when run
# from inside the work tree. 0.7.3 was published from a staging copy OUTSIDE the
# git work tree, where a repo-root .gitignore does not apply. Pub then included
# every file on disk and reported "Package has 0 warnings".
#
# `.pubignore` lives inside the package, so it travels wherever the package is
# copied, staged, or archived. It holds in exactly the condition where the
# repo-root .gitignore silently stops applying.
#
# Do not delete this file to "clean up". It is the countermeasure.

# Build output (the 0.7.3 defect).
build/

# Tooling / analysis artifacts.
.dart_tool/
coverage/
doc/api/

# Library packages do not ship a lockfile; consumers resolve their own.
pubspec.lock

# Scratch.
*.log
